<title>USA: TABLE - Enron Global Power Q2 profit rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Enron Global Power Q2 profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended June 30</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.50		    $0.48</p>
<p> Net			 12,999		   11,575</p>
<p> Revs			13,725		   14,609</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  26,001		   24,051</p>
<p>	   6 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.22		    $0.96</p>
<p> Net			 31,007		   23,096</p>
<p> Revs			29,102		   29,494</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  25,431		   24,024</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Full company name is Enron Global Power &amp; Pipelines LLC. It is a majority-owned unit of Enron Corp.</p>
<p>1997 Q2 includes a one-time, after-tax charge of $1.9 million, or $0.07 per share, for the reversal of an early completion bonus connected to the construction of a natural gas pipeline in Colombia. Excluding the charge, EPS were $0.57.</p>
</text>
